    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Resilience Facility (PRF) is a Pacific owned, led and designed initiative endorsed by Pacific Island Forum (PIF) Leaders to generate Pacific managed funds for small-scale climate resilience projects. During the reporting period Australia&#x2019;s contribution to the PRF supported establishment activities to formulate governance arrangements and country of domicile considerations. Once established, the PRF will enhance Pacific access to climate finance and fund climate change resilience initiatives in the Pacific region to reduce the vulnerability and exposure of Pacific communities to disaster risks, from climate change and other hazards.</narrative>
    </description>
